  "title": "AJILE12: long-term naturalistic ECoG with wrist-movement events and behaviour labels (DANDI 000055)",
  "description": "AJILE12 is a long-term naturalistic intracranial dataset of electrocorticography (ECoG) recorded opportunistically from 12 epilepsy patients during clinical monitoring at Harborview Medical Center. Recordings cover 55 full monitoring days (days 3-7 after implantation) with simultaneous video, from which upper-body pose, validated wrist-movement initiation events and coarse behavioural state labels were derived. This iEEG-BIDS representation converts the original NWB release from DANDI without altering signal values.",
  "methods_description": "Semi-continuous ECoG (1 kHz, released at 500 Hz after median DC removal, 1-200 Hz band-pass, 60 Hz notch and common median re-referencing) and 30 fps video were passively recorded during 24-hour clinical epilepsy monitoring. Electrodes were localised with FieldTrip by co-registering pre-operative MRI with post-operative CT and warping to MNI space. Wrist-movement events were detected from pose estimates and visually validated, and coarse behaviours were annotated manually.",
